+ * The RK356x NPU runs without an IOMMU ("using non-iommu mode"), so every
+ * buffer the RKNN userspace runtime hands to it has to be physically
+ * contiguous.  The upstream system heap allocates from a buddy page pool and
+ * can only guarantee contiguity inside a single order block (1MB/64K/4K), so
+ * any buffer larger than one block comes out scattered.  The RKNPU driver
+ * derives the hardware base address from the last scatterlist entry of the
+ * mapped sg_table, which for a scattered buffer is some page in the middle of
+ * the range, the NPU then fetches from a bogus address, never makes progress
+ * and the job times out with "core 0 .... task counter: 0x0".
+ *
+ * This heap keeps the exported heap name ("system", i.e. /dev/dma_heap/system,
+ * which the RKNN runtime opens by name) but backs every allocation with one
+ * physically contiguous block taken from the default CMA area.  That yields an
+ * sg_table with exactly one entry, so the address the driver reads is the true
+ * base of the contiguous buffer, exactly like the vendor rk_cma_heap /
+ * rk_system_heap stacks.
